#!/bin/sh
# Build qim and run it inside the development container with the devices and
# privileges it needs (KVM, tap devices, bind mounts, a packet socket for the
# capture). Images and outputs go to build/qim. The audit reader is found next
# to the qim binary.
set -eu
repo=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)
"$repo/dev/cargo" build --release --quiet
exec "$repo/dev/podman" run --rm \
  --device /dev/kvm --device /dev/net/tun --group-add keep-groups \
  --cap-add SYS_ADMIN --cap-add NET_ADMIN --cap-add NET_RAW --sysctl net.ipv4.ip_forward=1 \
  -v "$repo:/src:ro" -v "$repo/build:/work" \
  -e QIM_HOME=/work/qim -w /work \
  qim-dev /src/build/target/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/qim "$@"
